data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1226.txt-3-On a warrant issued by the Attorney General, an alien may be arrested and detained pending a decision on whether the alien is to be removed from the United States. Except as provided in subsection (c) and pending such decision, the Attorney General—
data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1226.txt-4-(1) may continue to detain the arrested alien; and
data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1226.txt:5:(2) may release the alien on—
data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1226.txt:6:(A) bond of at least $1,500 with security approved by, and containing conditions prescribed by, the Attorney General; or
data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1226.txt-7-(B) conditional parole; but
data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1226.txt-8-(3) may not provide the alien with work authorization (including an "employment authorized" endorsement or other appropriate work permit), unless the alien is lawfully admitted for permanent residence or otherwise would (without regard to removal proceedings) be provided such authorization.
data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1226.txt-9-The Attorney General at any time may revoke a bond or parole authorized under subsection (a), rearrest the alien under the original warrant, and detain the alien.
